--   - `productCharacter`: PDF pp.4,6: the character of an actual product basis vector, including the empty product.
--   - `productSymmetryMatrix`: PDF p.4: the actual system representation u(g) tensor n in the chosen product basis.
--   - `charges`: PDF p.20: only characters actually occurring in this tensor power are counted.
--   - `chargeCount`: PDF p.20: the number of distinct occurring characters, not the number of basis strings.
--   - `embedOnSites`: PDF p.4: embedding on any ordered list of distinct named sites, with identity outside it.
--   - `IsSupportedOnAtMost`: PDF p.4: acts on at most k sites; zero-site scalar operators are allowed.
--   - `CommutesWithSymmetry`: PDF p.4: symmetry means commutation with the specified tensor-power action at every g.
--   - `finiteGateProducts`: PDF p.4: exact finite products in temporal order; the empty word gives identity.
--   - `symmetricLocalGroup`: PDF p.4: the actual group generated by individually invariant local unitary gates.
--   - `derived`: PDF pp.5,19: the derived subgroup, generated by actual multiplicative commutators.
--   - `symmetricCircuitCommutant`: PDF p.6 Eq.(6): the full complex operator commutant.
--   - `blockPreservingUnitaries`: PDF pp.5,6: block-diagonality for a relation on the physical product basis.
--   - `blockSpecial`: PDF pp.5,6: determinant one independently on every whole physical block. Representatives may repeat a block; each determinant is taken on its full support.
--   - `sameCharge`: PDF p.6: equal charge means equality of complete character functions on all G.
--   - `SemiUniversal`: PDF p.5 Eq.(5): every independent charge-block special unitary is realizable.
--   - `NoExtra`: PDF p.6 Eq.(6), including the fixed second equality with the representation span.
--   - `CommDimension`: PDF p.6 Eq.(7): dimension of the complex commutant.
--   - `basisPath`: PDF pp.7,12: a finite path with both endpoints, allowing a one-vertex path.
--   - `TransitiveCharges`: PDF p.7 Theorem 2 prime, condition 3.
--   - `component`: PDF p.12 Eq.(28): canonical joint-eigenspace relation of the actual commutant. This is defined from the generated group, not from the desired basis paths.
--   - `componentSpace`: PDF p.12: the full physical span of one commutant-defined basis block.
--   - `InvariantSpace`: PDF p.12: invariance under every actually generated unitary.
--   - `ComponentDecomposition`: PDF pp.6,12: completeness, orthogonality, charge refinement and actual irreducibility.
--   - `reservoirLength`: PDF p.7 Eq.(13): the least positive reservoir length attaining the n-site charge count. For n positive the defining set contains n; no default infimum is used in a theorem.
--   - `leftRegularPermutationMatrix`: PDF p.7: left regular action, |h> maps to |g h>.
--   - `IsRegularOnsiteRepresentation`: PDF p.7: the chosen diagonal representation is unitarily equivalent to the regular one.
--   - `traceCharacter`: PDF pp.7,18: the actual trace character of one qudit.
--   - `localChargeSpan`: PDF pp.19-20: real span of the complete functions r^(n-k) f_mu on all G.
--   - `lieSpace`: PDF p.19: the actual Lie algebra, characterized by one-parameter subgroups. Its real linear span is used, never a freely supplied Lie-algebra dimension.
--   - `groupDimension`: PDF p.19: real Lie dimension of the actual generated subgroup.
--   - `CompactLie`: PDF p.18: a compact finite-dimensional real Lie group, with its actual topology.
--   - `cyclicPhases`: PDF pp.5,8: the specified Z_p qubit representation, on its actual residues. Only the values are needed to define commutation; no abstract charge labels are supplied.
--   - `excitationPhases`: PDF p.7: diag(1,z) for z on the unit circle, equivalent for invariance to z rotations.
--   - `residueCharge`: PDF p.8: total Z_p charge is excitation number modulo p.
--   - `basisMatrixUnit`: PDF p.13: the dyad |r><s| on the complete physical Hilbert space.
--   - `twoX`: PDF p.13: the two-level X operator, zero on every other basis vector.
--   - `twoY`: PDF p.13: the paper's Y has +i on |r><s|, hence is minus the usual ordered Pauli Y.
--   - `twoZ`: PDF p.13: Z = (i/2)[X,Y] = |r><r| - |s><s|.
--   - `positiveImaginaryEvolution`: PDF pp.8,13: the source's positive-sign exponential exp(i theta H).
--   - `RedistributionTransition`: PDF p.8: a redistribution dyad on at most k qudits, with its actual local basis labels.
--   - `transitionOps`: PDF p.8 Eq.(18): allowed embeddings of the Hermitian partial swaps, not permutation swaps.
--   - `Redistributes`: PDF p.8: R is invariant and acts transitively at the stated k-site scale.
--   - `czFamily`: PDF pp.8,14: all named-site two-qudit controlled phases from Eq.(37).
